  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Epi-actephilol A and SMMC-7721, mediated through the 5-(2-Hydroxyacetyl)-10H-Phenazine-1-Carboxylic Acid pathway. This compound is identified as a target of Epi-actephilol A in three distinct pathways, with varying scores (0.4793 to 0.4911), indicating a consistent but not absolute interaction. The pathway involves Epi-actephilol A acting as a modulator of a kinase involved in the activation of 5-(2-Hydroxyacetyl)-10H-Phenazine-1-Carboxylic Acid, which in turn targets SMMC-7721. This suggests that Epi-actephilol A may influence cellular processes in SMMC-7721 cells through this metabolic cascade. The evidence supports a functional link between Epi-actephilol A and SMMC-7721, but the exact mechanism and the strength of the interaction remain to be fully elucidated. The overlapping targets and the presence of a common downstream effector highlight the potential for Epi-actephilol A to exert its effects on SMMC-7721 via a shared signaling pathway.",
